    fix(node): bind brief.digest to every effectful field (CF-275)
    
    Scheme: cf-brief-v1 — sha256 over canonical JSON (sorted keys, `,`/`:` separators, UTF-8) of {scheme, text, gate{cmd,expect_exit,timeout_s}, repo, ref, workdir, vars}, so the gate.cmd that run_gate() hands to `/bin/sh -lc` is INSIDE the digest; brief_digest() and the sender CLI `--print-brief-digest <dispatch.json|->` are the one helper both sides use.
    Legacy rule: sha256(text) is still accepted on a brief carrying NO gate, and refused by the named `brief_digest` row once a gate is present — as is a gate with no digest at all: an executable the digest does not bind is never run.
    Fixture: tests/test_brief_digest_binding.py, wired as selftest §57 — B1 a bound brief runs its gate; B2 the same brief with ONLY gate.cmd altered is refused with the gate marker absent and the harness never started; B3 legacy digest beside a gate; B4 legacy without a gate; B5 gate without a digest; B6 pinned canonical bytes, per-member sensitivity and CLI agreement.
    Control: P0 points the SAME fixture at c05880d and requires the tampered gate to RUN there — it fails against the fixed worker, so the fixture discriminates instead of merely passing.
    Docs: specs/ENVELOPE.md states the cf-brief-v1 object, what it does not cover and the legacy rule; docs/OPERATIONS.md states the trust boundary (a node must not execute a field the digest does not bind); the skills/code-factory-bunker/SKILL.md refusal row is updated; docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md gains the §57 mapping row and the derived census (57 numbered sections, 60 arms) its CF-198 guard checks.
